#====================================================================
# E236 — Isolate non-relocatable Libtool dependency metadata
#====================================================================

id:                     E236
trigger_tool:           libtool|llvm-ar|autotools|conan
phase:                  linking|package|testing
error_signature:        library .*\.la was moved|is not a valid libtool archive|archive member .*\.a is neither ET_REL nor LLVM bitcode|undefined symbol: (pcre2_|sqlite3_)

severity:               2
category:               autotools|libtool|conan|static-linking
match_keywords:         Libtool, Conan, .la, libdir='//lib', library was moved, nested archive, ET_REL, llvm-ar, LIBADD, PCRE2_LIBS, SQLITE3_LIBS
title:                  Isolate non-relocatable Libtool dependency metadata

root_cause:             Libtool gives visible .la files precedence over sibling static archives. A relocated Conan
                        dependency can retain an invalid libdir or dependency_libs path in that metadata, so Libtool
                        follows a path that no longer exists. Passing the dependency as an absolute .a path is not
                        equivalent to a normal -l dependency when another Libtool static archive is being built:
                        llvm-ar can embed the complete dependency archive as a member, leaving the later executable
                        link with a non-ET_REL member and unresolved dependency symbols.
affected_scope:         Autotools and Libtool projects that consume static Conan dependencies whose lib directories
                        contain stale or non-relocatable .la files, especially when the project itself produces a
                        static Libtool archive.
verification_cmd:       Run a clean conan create, require the enabled upstream tests and a real package consumer to
                        pass on the target, inspect the target archive with llvm-ar t for nested dependency archives,
                        and require the final package to contain no unintended .la files.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           scoped-la-free-static-archive-directory
rec_description:        Copy only the required dependency .a files into a build-private directory that contains no .la
                        metadata. Pass that directory through the upstream dependency-scoped CFLAGS and LIBS variables
                        as -L<dir> -lname, leave the Conan dependency cache unchanged, and remove generated .la metadata
                        from the final package.
rec_command:            mkdir -p <build>/.dependency-archives; cp <dependency>/lib/libfoo.a <build>/.dependency-archives/; FOO_LIBS='-L<build>/.dependency-archives -lfoo' ./configure
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-recipe

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      regenerate-relocatable-libtool-metadata
fallback_description:   If a project genuinely requires public Libtool metadata, regenerate the dependency .la files
                        for the final install prefix and validate all dependency_libs entries instead of editing the
                        Conan cache in place.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          dependency-recipe

forbid_1_pattern:       rm .*\.la.*conan|sed .*libdir=.*\.la
forbid_1_reason:        Mutating the dependency package cache breaks immutability and can affect unrelated builds that share the same Conan package revision.
forbid_1_consequence:   Reproducibility depends on cache state outside the current recipe.

forbid_2_pattern:       [A-Za-z0-9_./-]+/lib[^ ]+\.a.*LIBADD
forbid_2_reason:        An absolute static archive passed through Libtool LIBADD can become a nested archive member instead of a link dependency.
forbid_2_consequence:   The final archive contains a non-ET_REL member and later links fail with unresolved dependency symbols.

principles:             P010, P012

causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

